{"content":"Found the bug: `IdentifierList.get_identifiers()` in sqlparse/sql.py has an inverted condition. The docstring says "Whitespaces and punctuations are not included in this generator," but the code yields tokens when they ARE whitespace or comma punctuation (backwards). This breaks many things that rely on get_identifiers (including the aligned indent filter's `_process_identifierlist`, which pops the first identifier and inserts newlines before the rest — now operating on whitespace/punctuation tokens instead of actual identifiers).

Fixing by negating the condition to match the documented contract, then verifying with the reported aligned-reindent SQL and other get_identifiers consumers.","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_1","name":"replace_text","arguments":{"path":"sqlparse/sql.py","old_text":"        for token in self.tokens:
